DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'MathObjects.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
TEXT(beginproblem());
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
$prompt = <<'PROMPT_4A7D_E9F0';
<p>4a7d_e9f0</p> <table border="0" style="border: 0px solid white; border-collapse: collapse; "><colgroup width="60"></colgroup> <colgroup width="60"></colgroup> <colgroup width="60"></colgroup> <tr><td></td><td align="center">Gene 1</td><td></td></tr><tr> <td align="center" style="background-color: sienna">brown</td> <td align="center">&xrarr;</td> <td align="center" style="background-color: yellow">yellow</td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center">Gene 2</td></tr></table><br/>When either gene 1 or gene 2 is dominant, they express an enzyme that converts the brown precursor pigment into the yellow pigment. If both gene 1 and gene 2 are homozygous recessive, then only the brown precursor pigment is present <br/> <br/><p>The diagram and description above explain the interaction of two genes. <b>Determine the dihybird cross phenotypic ratio.</b></p>
PROMPT_4A7D_E9F0
